WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Pakistan's air strikes on Afghan sites test mediation efforts that could affect stability across South Asia. This is Omni View, episode 185. Pakistan conducted air strikes on 10 locations in Afghanistan's coast province. Officials said those sites stored and launched drones. The strikes followed drone attacks on Pakistani territory the previous day. Afghan officials reported no casualties from the Pakistani action. An attack on a police

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.080
These facility in northwestern Pakistan last week killed at least 21 people and triggered

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.240
the latest round of cross-border violence.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.880
The factual ground both sides accept is that drone flights cross the border and strikes

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.220
hit specific sites inside Afghanistan.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:51.200
Pakistan's Information Minister described the strikes as deliberate, precise, and limited

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.900
to military targets linked to cross-border attacks.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.580
tax. Afghan authorities have denied harboring armed groups that stage attacks inside Pakistan

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:05.240
and have called the strikes a violation of sovereignty. The escalation comes after earlier

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:10.720
fighting in February that was the worst in years between the two neighbors. China, Turkey,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.100
Qatar, and Saudi Arabia have been attempting to broker a lasting peace between the former

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:22.000
allies. Al Jazeera reports detailed accounts of the location struck and the official statements

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.380
from both governments. The same outlet notes that regional mediation efforts continue despite

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:33.360
the latest exchange. Even supporters of Pakistan's action concede that further strikes risk drawing

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:40.000
in additional actors and complicating the mediation already underway. What happens next depends on whether

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.100
the four mediating countries can secure a pause in operations before winter sets in. The United States

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:52.060
States has not issued a visa to Sudanese Army Chief Abdel Fatah Al-Berhan for the UN General

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:57.860
Assembly. Reports indicate the reported condition is agreement to a 90-day ceasefire proposal.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.840
Neither the Sudanese government nor the U.S. State Department has commented on the reports.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.780
The Reuters news agency cited Sudanese sources saying the visa issuance was made contingent

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.240
on acceptance of the truce proposed by U.S. senior adviser Masad Bulos.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:19.200
Sudanese activists and journalists have described the reported move as improper political pressure

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.780
that should not link visa access to cease-fire positions.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:29.800
UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres expressed concern and urged the U.S. to meet its obligations

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.860
under the UN Headquarters agreement.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.960
Al Jazeera reports on activist reactions and diplomatic sources that frame the visa question

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.340
as a test of standard diplomatic practice.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.740
The Civil War has already produced the world's largest hunger and displacement crises.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:52.660
General Al-Berhan's army has been fighting the paramilitary rapid support forces since April 2023.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.840
Russian forces struck Kiev with ballistic missiles and drones,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.100
killing two people according to Ukrainian President Vladimir Zelensky.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.320
The attacks come as autumn approaches and Ukraine prepares for winter energy shortages.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:11.800
images. A series of blasts rocked the capital as residents braced for harsher conditions following

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:17.480
intensified strikes on power facilities. Ukrainian officials say the strikes targeted energy

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:22.960
infrastructure and civilian areas. Russian statements have framed the operations as responses

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:29.400
to Ukrainian actions. France 24 provides on-the-ground reporting from Kiev that documents damage

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:34.800
across multiple districts. The attacks follow a pattern of intensified strikes on power

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:40.320
facilities ahead of colder months. Indian authorities are extending restrictions on the sale of

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.860
certain high-fat, high-sugar products to shops located near schools. The measure builds on

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:50.580
earlier national guidelines aimed at reducing childhood consumption of processed foods.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:56.920
The policy targets outlets within a defined radius of educational institutions. Health officials

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.520
argue the step addresses rising rates of diet-related conditions among young people.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:08.120
Industry representatives have raised concerns about enforcement clarity and the impact on small retailers.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:14.960
Reuters reports the policy details and the timeline still being finalized by state-level food safety authorities.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.920
The policy aligns with similar efforts in other countries to limit children's access to certain products.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:28.740
Pakistan's new automotive rules keep requirements that manufacturers export 12% of vehicle value produced locally.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:34.300
The policy also ties export performance to licensing and import concessions.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:39.780
Japanese automakers have previously raised similar rules at the World Trade Organization.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:45.220
Chinese producers operating in Pakistan are positioned to meet the export thresholds

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.080
more readily under current conditions.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.060
Pakistani officials say the targets support domestic industry development and technology transfer.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:58.500
Japan's manufacturers and trade officials have argued the measure's function as de facto

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.300
local content requirements that distort trade.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:06.860
Nikkeh Asia provides analysis of the export rules and the differing positions of Japanese

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.040
and Chinese firms.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:14.320
Experts note that strict targets on exports remain in place while Chinese makers stand to benefit

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.120
from the framework.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:21.320
ASEAN ministers have set November as the target for signing the digital economy framework agreement

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:26.960
during the Manila Summit. The pact aims to create common rules across the 11 member block

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:32.620
for emerging digital sectors. Ministers reaffirmed commitment to the agreement to foster a more

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:38.280
integrated and inclusive region. Supporters within ASEAN describe the agreement as a way to

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:43.960
increase integration and attract investment in digital services. Some member states have emphasized

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.500
the need for inclusive provisions that accommodate differing levels of digital infrastructure.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:56.400
NICA Asia reports the timeline and the scope of the agreement that would establish baseline standards rather than full harmonization.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:05.840
What's actually being done in Germany is a published plan to phase out fossil fuels through accelerated electrification of transport, heating and industry.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:14.400
The 2045 target reaffirms an earlier climate commitment and includes specific milestones for renewable capacity and grid upgrades.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.560
The plan focuses on practical deployment steps rather than new legislation.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:24.800
Industry groups have noted the scale of required infrastructure investment while environmental

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.700
organizations have welcomed the clarity on timelines.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.620
Deutsche Wella details the electrification measures and the targets that will guide implementation.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:39.660
Implementation will depend on permitting speed and supply chain availability for key technologies.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:39.840
communities.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:45.540
To really understand how cross-border responses are calibrated when both sides claim defensive

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:50.040
necessity, consider the legal language governments use under the UN charter.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:56.200
States often describe actions as proportionate and limited to identified military objectives

00:06:56.200 --> 00:07:00.320
to stay within the language of self-defense while avoiding wider war.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:06.880
Pakistan's statement at the strikes were deliberate, precise, calibrated, and proportionate, follows

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.420
this established pattern seen in multiple prior border incidents.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:16.040
The split is whether those sites hosted groups actively planning attacks or were unrelated

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:16.780
facilities.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.420
Knowing this framing helps readers separate the legal claim each government is making from

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.320
the underlying evidence of who controls which territory.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:31.280
Historical cases from other border regions show that such calibrated language often precedes

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.620
renewed mediation attempts rather than open escalation.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:41.360
The pattern appears in multiple documented incidents where precise wording preserved room for third-party involvement.

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:47.740
When the next report appears, check whether either side has offered independent verification of the target's

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:51.100
struck or invited outside observers to assess the sites.

